<%# Opening the doorbell #592 adds, and answering it. The argument, including why it carries no
    markup of its own, is in lib/tectonic/session_stream.rb.

    Outside #session-body for the reason everything stateful on this screen is: that region is
    replaced on every tap and every poll, and an open connection is state. It reads the poller
    for where to connect and which fingerprint to ask about, rather than being rendered with
    either, because the poller is the one element that is always current about both -- it
    replaces itself on every swap for exactly that reason.

    A `changed` event fires the poll, by the same route the write queue already uses to ask it
    for news early (`queue-drained`); the poll does the rest, and answers 204 if a swap already
    brought the screen up to date. The stream is closed first and reopened a second later, by
    which time the poller has usually been replaced and carries the new fingerprint -- and if
    not, the worst case is one more doorbell answered by one more 204.

    A failed connection backs off, doubling to half a minute, and a clean `done` reconnects at
    once. A hidden tab holds no connection: a phone locked on this screen is a server thread
    held for nobody, and the poll catches the screen up the moment it is looked at again.
    Without EventSource none of this runs, and the fifteen-second poll is the whole story, as it
    was before. %>
<script>
  (function () {
    if (!window.EventSource) { return; }
    var source = null;
    var timer = null;
    var failures = 0;

    function poller() { return document.getElementById('session-poll'); }

    function address() {
      var poll = poller();
      return poll && poll.getAttribute('hx-get').replace('/session/changes?', '/session/stream?');
    }

    function close() {
      if (source) { source.close(); source = null; }
      clearTimeout(timer);
    }

    function later(delay) {
      close();
      timer = setTimeout(connect, delay);
    }

    function connect() {
      var url = address();
      if (document.hidden || !url) { return; }
      source = new EventSource(url);
      source.addEventListener('changed', function () {
        failures = 0;
        document.body.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('session-changed'));
        later(1000);
      });
      source.addEventListener('done', function () {
        failures = 0;
        later(0);
      });
      source.onerror = function () {
        failures += 1;
        later(Math.min(30000, 1000 * Math.pow(2, failures)));
      };
    }

    document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', function () {
      if (document.hidden) { close(); } else { later(0); }
    });
    later(0);
  })();
</script>
